WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:04.270
The year is 2205 A.D.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:13.860
To annihilate the History Retrograde Army,
who scheme to alter history...

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.620
...we, who were born from swords,

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.210
engage in mortal combat today as well!

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:47.770
"Touken Ranbu Hanamaru S2"

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:01.800
Master, look at this vegetable!

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.220
What do you think? Aren't you surprised?

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:11.810
"This anime is about the
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.300
of a certain group of
Sword Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.530
Souza, do you have a minute?

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:25.290
Come on, hurry up.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.250
Jeez, what is it?

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:31.540
"Fudou"      "Ama"

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:32.170
This Sword Warrior just arrived at the citadel.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.710
He has the same former
master as you, right, Souza?

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.210
Oh my.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.300
Hey!

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.130
Are you Souza?

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:41.680
Long time no see.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.350
A new sword?

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.890
One of Oda Nobunaga's swords,
like you, Nii-<i>sama</i>?

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.980
Yup, that's right!

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.060
I'm Fudou Yukimitsu.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.600
"52 - Tantou, Fudou Yukimitsu"

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.770
I'm a masterpiece that
Lord Nobunaga loved very much.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.650
How much?

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:02.110
So much that when he got drunk, he would
slap his knees and sing, boasting about me.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:04.160
That's a lot, don't you think?

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.660
Yes, I suppose.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:10.500
But I'm a useless sword that
couldn't protect Nobunaga-<i>sama</i>, though.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:14.540
New fertilizer?

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:15.790
Sounds interesting.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.550
It will soon be the rainy season.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.170
We must make sure
Master's herbs do not wither.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.630
Hasebe! Yagen!

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.930
Another Oda sword is here.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.140
Yagen... Toushirou?

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.730
Fudou Yukimitsu?

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.810
You've come to this citadel, too?

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.230
So, who's he?

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.480
You don't know?

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.490
Hasebe's the one
Oda Nobunaga gave to Kuroda--

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:43.610
My name is Heshikiri Hasebe.
I was the second sword to come to--

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:44.950
Kuroda?!

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:49.370
You were given to someone who wasn't
even an immediate retainer of Nobunaga-<i>sama</i>?

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.540
And "Heshikiri"?

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.290
What a weird name!

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:54.120
What?!

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.420
Kashuu, what's up with this guy?

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:57.920
Don't ask me.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:02.720
But the name "Heshikiri" was given
to him by Lord Nobunaga, you know.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.300
Really? By Nobunaga-<i>sama</i>?

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.100
I don't care about that guy.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.020
Just hearing his name is unpleasant.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.310
What did you say?!

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:15.270
Listen. Your master is
not Oda Nobunaga anymore.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:19.230
Now that you've come to this citadel,
you must serve your current master.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.740
Nobunaga-<i>sama</i> is the one I care about!

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:23.610
What? You little…

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.490
Now, now. Calm down.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.080
This is...

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.240
I worry about what is to come...

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.500
Hey, newbie!

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.210
Would you like to chat with us?

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.970
We have snacks we got from Master, too.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:45.550
No thanks, I'll pass.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:52.640
Oh, I wonder if there are any snacks here...

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.440
Hey, Fudou-<i>kun</i>.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.190
We're making <i>zunda mochi</i> right now.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.610
Do you want to make them with us?

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.270
They're delicious!

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:03.190
We'll bring some over to Master later, too.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:05.700
If a useless sword like me makes them,

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.740
then even delicious food will taste bad.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.370
Did something happen?

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:19.250
I finished it...

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.460
Ow!

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:25.800
"Come In"

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:26.050
Who put this at my feet?!

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.090
What's this?

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:28.390
"Come In"

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.560
Welcome!

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.430
Oh, you must be a new sword.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.020
Now, come in, come in!

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.390
What'll you drink?

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.310
"Ama"

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.360
I'm just a useless sword, after all.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:46.150
But Nobunaga-<i>sama</i>
still treasured me so much.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.660
What's wrong with liking him?!

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:55.160
Fudou-<i>chan</i>, you really
love Oda Nobunaga, huh?

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.580
Of course!

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.170
Nobunaga-<i>sama</i> was amazing, you know!

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:03.800
But that bastard Hasebe
called him "that guy."

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.420
And everyone else just keeps
going on and on about "Master."

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:09.720
It's pretty good that he even talked about him.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.220
Even though the Kuroda family
took care of him for a long time,

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:17.180
he doesn't talk about them at all.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.520
Now that you mention it, I don't think
I've ever heard him talk about them.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.690
Don't you think he's just not interested
in anything other than his current master?

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:27.070
Now, now. When you're
feeling gloomy, you should drink up!

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.030
How long are you guys
going to keep up this racket?

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:30.860
Hasebe-<i>kun</i>, welcome!

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:32.320
What's this room?

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.080
Hasebe-<i>kun</i>, how about a drink?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.160
No thanks.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.870
Hey, Hasebe.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:40.620
Why don't you ever talk
about the Kuroda family?

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.330
Because I don't want to talk about them.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:45.750
Come on, tell us.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:49.260
Are you saying you can't tell us
because I'm a useless sword?

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:51.720
I want to hear about it, too.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:54.760
Nagamasa-<i>sama</i> was a good man.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.600
If artifact spirits could go to the next world,
I would've wanted to follow him there.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:03.810
But we cannot. We remain
in this world longer than humans.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.940
That's why I decided to forget.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.900
Is that right?

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:11.910
Because my current master
is the most important!

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.580
After I went through
all the trouble of answering,

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.330
how could you fall asleep?!

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:21.500
Hey!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.710
That's the dango I got from Master!

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:28.550
Sorry, sorry. They were out,
so I thought it was okay to eat--

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:30.760
I can't believe you!

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:33.890
Yasusada, don't you think
you're being too gluttonous?

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:35.510
You don't have to call me a glutton!

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:38.560
But I got them from Master!

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:46.480
Kashuu!

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.070
Do you know where Fudou is?

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.190
Is something the matter?

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:52.320
We're getting dispatched to
Azuchi Castle, but I can't find him.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.200
What's the team? Am I on it?

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:59.580
"Sa"

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:59.870
No, this time, it's Heshikiri Hasebe,
Souza Samonji, Yagen Toushirou,

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:04.380
Fudou Yukimitsu, and Jiroutachi,
with me as the captain.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:05.710
I see.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.920
Fudou went to the roof earlier.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.550
Really? Thanks.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.590
I wasn't chosen again...

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.560
I'm behind you!

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:31.400
When I rage, I'm like a storm!

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:41.500
That's where Nobunaga-<i>sama</i>...

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:49.340
You cannot avoid...

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.050
...my blade!

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:53.760
Was that the last of them?

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:58.100
He's...!

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.600
Nobunaga-<i>sama</i>...

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.600
What are you doing?!

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:09.480
Bastard, what were you trying to do?

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:14.950
Even though I was treasured by
Nobunaga-<i>sama</i>, I couldn't protect him.

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:18.660
But I might be able to help him now.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:20.120
So...

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:23.330
Your master right now is not Oda Nobunaga.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:27.290
Carrying out our current
master's orders is our duty.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:28.830
Shut up!

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:32.340
Even if you tell me that all
of a sudden, I can't accept it!

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.720
Just what I'd expect from a useless sword!

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.850
Yeah, I'm just a useless sword, after all.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.430
What's the matter with him?!

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:47.230
He's just awkward.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:50.810
He just manifested,
so it's no wonder that he's confused.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:55.490
I know. But if he disturbs the peace,
then it'll affect everyone.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.110
That's true.

00:09:57.110 --> 00:10:01.660
But don't you think
you also went a little too far?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:06.580
"Fudou Yukimitsu, my Tsukumo-nasu teapot,

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:10.750
and my loyal retainer Gorozaemon
are my three treasures."

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:32.770
Nobunaga... <i>sama</i>...

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.610
Hey, have you seen Fudou?

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:43.490
Fudou? I saw him walking at the beach.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:46.330
Don't tell me he hasn't come back yet?

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:47.960
What did you say?

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:49.710
He...

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.670
Fudou!

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:56.050
Jeez, where did he go?

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:59.010
Hey! Isn't that Fudou?

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:04.390
We have to hurry and save him!

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:05.720
Please, wait.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:08.480
It's dangerous to swim when it's this dark.

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:14.900
I will go!

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.400
Please use these.

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.610
Thanks, I will!

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.030
Fudou!

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.540
Let's go home.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:33.330
No.

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:34.960
What?

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:39.720
I'm a useless sword that couldn't
return the love my master had for me.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:43.930
It's better if someone
like me isn't at that citadel!

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:48.270
Can you not see those guys over there?

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:48.970
You okay?

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:51.980
--Everyone was looking for you
because they were worried!
--Hurry up and come back!

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:54.730
Why would they do that for someone like me?

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:57.980
Because you're our comrade in this citadel.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:11.540
Welcome back!

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.580
Th-Thanks...

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.130
Here, hurry up and dry off.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:16.960
The bath's ready for you!

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.050
I'm glad you are okay.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:24.800
"Amazake"

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:23.380
Hurry up and come in! I've prepared
some warm <i>amazake</i> for you, too.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:27.050
All right, time for a celebratory drink!
We're drinking lots tonight!

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:30.020
You guys should restrain yourselves a little.

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:37.270
You're still awake?

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:39.980
I woke up for some reason.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:44.450
This citadel really is filled with good guys.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:50.370
They even gave a useless sword
like me a warm welcome.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:55.290
It's not your fault that that man died.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.710
When people are born,
they must die someday.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:00.800
Oda Nobunaga was no exception.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:04.590
I was given away.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:10.430
But by fulfilling my duty as a Sword Warrior,
I am also protecting that man's history.

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:12.310
It's ironic.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:17.270
In other words, if I protect history,
then it will help Nobunaga-<i>sama</i>?

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.610
Yeah, that's how it is.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:24.570
Hey, do you think I can love our current
master as much as I love Nobunaga-<i>sama</i>?

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.660
That's up to you.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:32.370
Tell me, what's the master here like?

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.170
A mysterious person
whose thoughts are inscrutable.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:40.710
But kind, and always thinking of us.

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:44.670
Not very good at keeping things
organized, and a homebody.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:50.180
But I keep their room clean, and I bring what
they want to their room, so it's no problem...

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:58.440
It's a good thing the cherry blossoms
bloomed after the storm.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:02.480
If the cherry blossoms fell off, then we
would not be able to have a viewing party.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:06.450
Speaking of which--

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:07.570
Hmm?

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:12.370
After that storm,
did you and Hasebe make up?

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:13.870
Who knows?

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.580
We're done laying it out!

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:19.420
Then... let's commemorate
that with a drink!

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:20.830
--Oh, good idea!
--What kind of commemoration is that?

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:23.750
Aren't you looking forward to
cherry blossom viewing, Nakigitsune?

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.460
Yeah.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:30.010
Oh, what kind of sword's coming this time?

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.140
"Sa"

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:42.440
My name is Kogarasumaru.

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.150
"53 - Tachi, Kogarasumaru"

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:44.940
Hey, I'm Shishiou!

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.950
And this guy's Yamanbagiri Kunihiro!

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:50.030
Nice to meet you!

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:53.490
You should not judge
someone by their appearance.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:59.080
I am a sword from the time when the
current form of Japanese swords was born.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:03.790
The father of all the swords here, so to speak.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.420
You may revere me as a father.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:10.930
Well, um, I've got my old man!

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:12.050
"Old man"?

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:16.220
Yeah, my old master, Minamoto no Yorimasa!

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:18.640
I love my old man!

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:22.400
I see. Why do you say that?

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:26.610
My old man's smooth and fluffy and warm!

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:28.240
He knows a bunch of stuff, too!

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.570
Fluffy?

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.450
I see...

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.990
What they call the wisdom of age, huh?

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:39.660
In that case, this father is
worth revering as your "old man."

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:42.460
We got a strange one this time, huh?

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:43.540
What should we do?

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:47.050
Let's take him to Kashuu, since he's
supposed to look after the newcomers.

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.590
Where's Kashuu?

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:51.300
Right now, he's outside getting
ready for cherry blossom viewing.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.300
All right, I'll leave it to you then.

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:54.850
What?

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.220
You come, too.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:56.930
Huh?

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:58.810
Did you just say "cherry blossom viewing"?

00:15:58.810 --> 00:15:59.850
Yeah...

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:02.810
This father does not dislike alcohol.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:05.520
Come now, let us go.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.940
Shishiou-<i>san</i>! Yamanbagiri-<i>san</i>!

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:09.820
Oh, a new friend?

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.610
I'm Kogarasumaru.

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:14.280
You may revere me as a father.

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.570
Father?!

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:19.790
Apparently, he is a sword who could be
called the father of all us Sword Warriors.

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:21.410
Our father?

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:23.040
Father-<i>sama</i>?

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.000
"Father-<i>sama</i>"?

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.290
Come, shall we go cherry blossom viewing?

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:30.010
Yeah, we were on our way, too!

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.300
Then, let us go.

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:36.680
Yes, Father-<i>sama</i>!

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:43.980
Are we ready?

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:48.320
Stop! Stop what you're doing!

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:51.280
Know who this personage is!

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:57.280
He is the Father-<i>sama</i> of us
Sword Warriors, Kogarasumaru!

00:16:57.280 --> 00:17:00.160
You may revere me as a father.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.460
May we also participate in
the cherry blossom viewing?

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:08.710
Of course! Come on, you attendants in
the back should hurry up and sit down, too.

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:11.010
We're not his attendants.

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:12.090
Now, then--

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.550
Cheers!

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:18.350
Here.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:19.810
I will pour for you.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:20.640
Huh?

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:23.060
Children should be spoiled by their fathers.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:27.310
I'm usually the one taking care
of others, so it feels a little weird.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.940
Well, it's the long-awaited
cherry blossom viewing.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:32.940
Will there be any entertainment?

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:33.940
Huh?

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:37.870
Oh, entertainment? That'd be great!

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:42.040
Everyone, how about we fire
things up with some entertainment

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:45.250
so we can welcome Kogarasumaru, too!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:47.420
That sounds fun!

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:51.130
Alrighty then, I'll be the top batter!

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:56.380
Here I go!

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.310
Wow, amazing!

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:02.890
I'm not done yet!

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.900
Yo! Nice, Mutsunokami!

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.900
How delightful.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.940
Alrighty, now for my greatest trick!

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:19.620
That's amazing!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:28.120
This is Tosa's Manly Giant Swing!

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:32.250
Alrighty, who's next?

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:40.970
And now, Kousetsu-<i>niisama</i>
will write some calligraphy.

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:43.430
I see, calligraphy, huh?

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:47.890
He will be writing, not on paper,
but on this grain of rice.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.110
I am finished.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:19:01.620
"When a blind turtle finds driftwood
When an udumbra flower blooms
I have been waiting for as long"

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.110
He wrote a poem!

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:01.910
I wrote it for Osayo.

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:03.700
Kousetsu-<i>niisama</i>...

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:04.910
Thanks.

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:07.500
Isn't that great, Osayo?

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.540
Will you do something?

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:12.540
Oh, you'll perform something too, Brother?

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:15.130
Then, let's do something together, Brother!

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:16.880
No, I...

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:22.390
Now, come and watch the entertainment
by the three Kunihiro brothers!

00:19:22.850 --> 00:19:25.100
First up is me!

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.810
Headbutt!

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:31.440
Next is me!

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:34.480
Look!

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.780
And...

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:43.490
Look!

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:46.540
Yo! As expected of Kunihiro!

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.330
Now, Brother!

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.160
Do your best next!

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:52.670
I know that I've grown...

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:55.670
I can do it... I'm sure I can!

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:02.010
Everyone, we brought
another round of food!

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:05.510
Yamanbagiri-<i>san</i>,
are you about to do something?

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:07.720
Huh?

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:12.020
No... Um...

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:23.110
I couldn't do anything exciting...

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:26.080
I guess I can't do anything
after all, since I'm a copy.

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:28.910
Yamanbagiri, don't worry about it!

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:33.330
What's up, Kogarasumaru?

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:38.550
As thanks for everyone's entertainment,
this father will dance a dance.

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:03.070
Huh?

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:06.620
You'll be fine if you're with Father, right?

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:09.200
Now, let's dance.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:30.350
Oh, Yamanbagiri-<i>kun</i>'s pretty good!

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.430
Great! Great!

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:37.310
Yes, you have aptitude for this.

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:41.110
That guy... For Yamanbagiri...

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:43.990
Huh? I'm fine!

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:46.950
You're an attendant, aren't you? Attend me.

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:49.120
I told you, I'm not an attendant!

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:57.920
Everyone gets along very well in this citadel.

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:01.420
Yeah, I guess. I hope we can get along, too!

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:11.640
They bloomed properly
this year, too, Yasusada.

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:15.730
Are you doing well?

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:01.590
"More <i>Hanamaru</i> Next Week!!"
